<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Abacan eases.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Abacan eases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian oil company Abacan Resource Corp eased lower Wednesday to stand out among American Depositary Receipts  ADRs and foreign shares.</p>
<p>Shares in the Calgary-based company were off 3/32 to 2-7/32. Volume was heavy at 5.9 million shares in late afternoon, and Abacan was the most-active foreign share.</p>
<p>Calgary-based Abacan fell more than 50 percent Monday after it said its 1997 cash flow would be much lower than analysts' predictions.  </p>
<p>Among other active foreign shares, Israel's ESC Medical Systems Ltd was off 2-7/8 to 21-1/2.</p>
<p>Nordic telecoms Telefon AB L.M. Ericsson and Nokia Group rose after market sources said Merrill Lynch raised its 1997 and 1998 earnings-per-share forecasts for the companies.</p>
<p>Ericsson rose 1-1/16 to 37-9/16 and Nokia was up 1-7/8 to 70-1/4.  Both companies were above their 12-month highs.</p>
